# UST.G3BV H02 Endpoint GF(11) Calibration

## Status

`CLOSED_EXACT_INDEPENDENT_CRT_ALIAS_REJECTION`

## Theorem

Rebuild the corrected selected G3BI H02 endpoint at

```text
(p, gamma) = (11, 3).
```

Exact sparse factorization finds selected column `42384` dependent, so the
endpoint determinant is `0 mod 11`. By contrast, the centered eight-prime
G3BU CRT candidate evaluates to `2 mod 11` at the same root.

Hence the eight-prime centered candidate is not the characteristic-zero
determinant. This independently confirms the G3BU holdout failure.

## Boundary

This result also shows that the older B89/F1 `GF(11)` inverse certificate
cannot be transferred to the corrected G3BI endpoint. It does not contradict
characteristic-zero invertibility, which is already certified at the separate
proof place `(21817,5)` with determinant `419`.

